  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "3.2.2 - Bug fixes, C# 14 modernization, and dependency refresh for .NET 10\n\n    This maintenance release hardens the library with targeted bug fixes, modernizes\n    internals with .NET 10 / C# 14 idioms, and refreshes all dependencies to their\n    latest stable versions. Fully backwards compatible with 3.2.1.\n\n    Bug fixes:\n    - Cancellation is now propagated (OperationCanceledException) by\n      FunctionalExtensions.Bind/Map for Task<Fin<T>> instead of being swallowed as a\n      failure, matching the Option/Seq overloads.\n    - SqlConnection instances created by the DI registrations\n      (AddFunctionalMsSqlDapper / AddFunctionalMsSql<TContext>) are now registered as\n      scoped services so the container disposes them, fixing a connection leak in\n      long-running applications.\n    - Error.New(string) now throws ArgumentNullException on a null message, preventing\n      a NullReferenceException in Error.GetHashCode().\n    - QueryResults.TotalPages no longer overflows for large TotalCount values.\n    - Dapper retry events are now attached to the operation's own activity instead of\n      Activity.Current, keeping retry telemetry correctly attributed.\n\n    C# 14 / .NET 10 modernization (non-breaking):\n    - Replaced the custom chunking iterator in EfFunctionalDb with Enumerable.Chunk.\n    - Seq<T>.Filter now uses ImmutableArrayBuilder.MoveToImmutable (no extra copy).\n    - QuerySpecification<T>.Includes now returns a cached read-only view.\n    - FunctionalMsSqlDb backend validation extracted to a static guard method.\n    - The xUnit v3 test suite now runs on Microsoft Testing Platform (xunit.v3 4.0.0).\n\n    Updated packages:\n    - Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore 10.0.11\n    - Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.SqlServer 10.0.11\n    - Microsoft.Data.SqlClient 7.0.2\n    - Dapper 2.1.79\n    - Microsoft.Extensions.Logging 10.0.11\n    - Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions 10.0.11\n    - Microsoft.Extensions.Options 10.0.11\n    - Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection.Abstractions 10.0.11\n\n    Fully backwards compatible with 3.2.1.\n    Safe drop-in upgrade.",
